    "introduction": "Shell operates across the energy supply chain, from producing oil and natural gas to supplying fuels, lubricants and electricity to customers. Its liquefied natural gas activities connect gas-producing regions with international markets, while refineries, chemical plants, trading operations and branded service stations provide further routes to market. Revenue comes from selling energy and related products to households, transport operators and industrial customers. The combination of production, processing and distribution gives Shell several sources of earnings, although each responds differently to commodity prices. Large projects, maintenance requirements and changing energy demand make capital allocation and operating reliability central to its business.",
